+    "C39a (Administration: AI Runtime Security end to end; C39b ports the other products and the review sheet on the same pattern). The chunk's work is committed on branch c39-admin at HEAD (the pre-gate commit aa95f632 and the check fixes 640103e7; BASE_REF=1ff6fe17) in its own worktree branched from main's C38 commit 1ff6fe17, so the C38 gate on main stayed in scope; scope and diff.patch are measured from 1ff6fe17. The owner's uncommitted build files (xtask sources, Cargo.lock, the Tauri manifests, the desktop-core version bump, the harness pin, the legacy feature views) are present as uncommitted copies, excluded from scope as the owner's work. Native acceptance C39-N01 and C39-N04 recorded against the rebuilt fixture bundle (native-prepare.json; executable hash bound in native-acceptance.json) with AX trees, self-captures and the measured layout matrix under evidence/C39/screens; C39-N02 (the review sheet) and C39-N03 (the other products) are C39b's checks and are not claimed here.",
+    "Visual parity (D059, docs/planning/p09-recut.md): the composites under docs/planning/evidence/C39/parity (prototype board left, fixture app right, captured by the native script after the tenant's read with AI Runtime Security open on Custom topics) were judged by the owner (parity/notes.md records the judgement and the deviations); the review scores the implementation against the chunk brief and the specification, not the pixels.",
