+# C44 remediation after attempt-01 (9/8/9/7/8: B1 predecessor record, R1–R4, E1 cumulative evidence)
+
+| Finding | Remediation | Where |
+|---|---|---|
+| B1 C43's review record is absent | Structural: C43's gate runs ahead of C44's attempt-02 in the queue (its first native runs stopped on driver and layout faults, since fixed); attempt-02's packet names its record. The ledger waits on C26 (status.md, P09 ledger note). | queue order |
+| R1 (P1) `tenant_on_home` saved the scan key and the management client before making the new tenant active; the core keeps the active tenant on create (the wizard's placeholder), so the credentials attached to it and every driver ran its tenant without them | Each tenant the driver creates is made active before its credentials are saved; every setup step's result is checked and a missing one stops the run. A pre-P09 driver gets the same through `legacy_v2.py` (activate-on-create). | `tools/native-acceptance/v2_setup.py`, `legacy_v2.py` |
+| R2 (P1) the legacy-script map grouped scripts under replacement ids; C10's dictionary/file-selection, C11's protected reveal/cache/export/isolation and C23's import/restart/rollback checks were mapped to checks that only open a destination | The map is assertion-level, generated from `native-checks.json`: every legacy check id, what it asserts, where it is asserted on the one presentation, and its result on the C44 bundle (`legacy_map.py`). The C10, C11 and C23 drivers themselves run on the one presentation through `legacy_v2.py` (the wizard's placeholder before Settings, activate-on-create, the Go menu for the legacy sidebar entries) and keep their own check ids; the C35–C43 drivers run again on the C44 bundle. Their records live under `native/cumulative/<CNN>/` (`run_on_v2.py`) and C44-N01 requires every one of them, bound to the prepared executable. | `legacy-script-map.md`, `legacy_map.py`, `run_on_v2.py`, `legacy_v2.py`, `acceptance_c44.py` |
+| R3 (P2) the DLP authoring suite was deleted and the management-client suite excluded while their components stay mounted | Both suites run on the one presentation: `v2/admin/dlp-authoring.test.tsx` (the Runtime card's DLP tab; v1's actions per inventory, the dictionary draft, a file by its token only, replace on edit, typed keywords kept on a cancelled or failed choice, one-JSON-object metadata) and `v2/settings/management-credential.test.tsx` (the secret cleared before awaiting and kept out of storage, required fields, the TSG requirement, the SSO pointer, one verification read with faithful failures, removal of the management client only). The owner's uncommitted legacy suite stays excluded, unedited. | the two suites, `vitest.config.ts` |
+| R4 (P2) `product_opened` passed on the product's name alone; the record claimed 1440×900 | A product counts as opened only when its card's Collapse control and its Overview tab are present; the record states the window and viewport actually captured (1440×811 inside 1440×843 on this display) against the 1440×900 request. | `acceptance_c44.py` |
+| E1 destination-opening smoke coverage only | The cumulative records above (the mapped drivers on this bundle) are the evidence; C44-N01 fails without them. | `acceptance_c44.py`, chain |
+| S run-checks.sh's fixture-command label | Corrected to `ui_v2_closure`. | `evidence/C44/runs/run-checks.sh` |
+| S the API Client's conversion report on tab changes | Not changed in this generation (optional; C41's scope). | — |
+
+Commands: `npx tsc --noEmit` clean; `npx vitest run` (apps/desktop) passes with the two ported suites. Attempt-02 (rebuild, the cumulative drivers, native, checks, packet, Codex) runs through the queue after C43's gate.
+
+Owner's dependency amendment, 2026-10-30 (approved in the owner's words: "Dependency amendment approved. go go go", to the statement "P09 chunks are reviewed on their own worktrees from each predecessor's pre-gate commit; predecessor remediation is integrated by the merge chain and validated by the P09 phase review"): a chunk's review takes the predecessor's record as it stands and does not require the predecessor's later remediation in its own tree.
